message:
feat: Support `ResponseSpec(..., examples=[...])` (#3100)

feat: Support `ResponseSpec(..., examples=[...])` (#3068)

Allows to define custom examples for the responses via `ResponseSpec`.

The examples set this way are always generated locally, for each response:

```json
{
    "paths": {
    "/": {
        "get": {
        "responses": {
            "200": {
            "content": {
                "application/json": {
                "schema": {...},
                "examples": ...
```

Examples that go within the schema definition cannot be set by this.

fix(dto): handle dto type nested in mapping (#3486)

Added handling for transferring data from a transfer model, to a DTO supported instance when the DTO supported type is nested in a mapping.

I.e, handles this case:

```py
@h287988ba06ef059c
class NestedDC:
    a: int
    b: str

@h287988ba06ef059c
class DC:
    nested_mapping: Dict[str, NestedDC]
```

Closes #3463
